1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:08,179
This video shows you how to send your fleet's own logs and metrics to the platform you already watch.

2
00:00:08,179 --> 00:00:10,310
Here, that's Elasticsearch.

3
00:00:10,360 --> 00:00:14,594
First, store the Elasticsearch API key as a secret.

4
00:00:14,594 --> 00:00:17,790
In Admin, open Secrets, and add one.

5
00:00:17,840 --> 00:00:19,810
Name it elastic-api-key.

6
00:00:19,810 --> 00:00:22,273
Its value lives on the leader.

7
00:00:22,273 --> 00:00:25,008
Paste the key, and add it.

8
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:31,451
In Build, open Sources, and add a source.

9
00:00:31,451 --> 00:00:36,851
Local, each worker, holds two: smeltr logs and smeltr metrics.

10
00:00:36,851 --> 00:00:39,350
Each runs on every worker.

11
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:42,851
Add smeltr metrics, as fleet-metrics.

12
00:00:44,360 --> 00:00:47,277
Then add smeltr logs, as fleet-logs.

13
00:00:47,277 --> 00:00:50,550
It keeps lines at info and above.

14
00:00:57,280 --> 00:01:01,069
Save them on a new branch, fleet-telemetry.

15
00:01:04,720 --> 00:01:09,349
Open Destinations, and add an Elasticsearch destination.

16
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:12,919
Name it fleet-es.

17
00:01:12,919 --> 00:01:18,070
Enter its URL, and the index to write to, smeltr-fleet.

18
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:22,897
This Elasticsearch has a certificate from your organization's own authority.

19
00:01:22,897 --> 00:01:26,070
Paste that authority under trusted authorities.

20
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:31,262
For the credential, choose an API key, and pick the secret you stored.

21
00:01:31,262 --> 00:01:33,111
Add it, and save.

22
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:38,186
Open Routes, and add a route.

23
00:01:38,186 --> 00:01:40,291
It starts from fleet-metrics.

24
00:01:40,291 --> 00:01:42,852
Make a new pipeline for it.

25
00:01:45,640 --> 00:01:49,981
Capture a sample from fleet-metrics, to see its records.

26
00:01:58,040 --> 00:02:02,424
smeltr proposes a Parser step that reads each record as JSON,

27
00:02:02,424 --> 00:02:05,011
and that is all this pipeline needs.

28
00:02:05,011 --> 00:02:07,590
Call it fleet-parse, and save it.

29
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:10,081
Add route picked tutorial-out.

30
00:02:10,081 --> 00:02:14,262
Take it off, and send the route to fleet-es.

31
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:20,653
Add a second route, for fleet-logs, through fleet-parse, to fleet-es.

32
00:02:20,653 --> 00:02:22,043
Then save.

33
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:32,116
Open it for review, then approve and deploy it.

34
00:02:32,116 --> 00:02:35,137
Both workers run the new commit.

35
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:57,212
In Kibana, Discover shows the records arriving in smeltr-fleet.

36
00:02:58,880 --> 00:03:05,361
A log carries its level, class, type and message, and the worker that wrote it.

37
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:19,073
A metric carries its name and value, and labels such as the destination it measures.

38
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:31,857
Check on learning.

39
00:03:32,057 --> 00:03:36,275
Which sources give your fleet's own logs and metrics?

40
00:03:40,675 --> 00:03:46,328
smeltr logs and smeltr metrics, under Local, each worker.

41
00:03:47,228 --> 00:03:50,953
Next, get alerted when something breaks.
